for the most unique and ancient site in  all of sri lanka you'll need to look up  way way up  [Music]  located 660 feet on top of a rock  plateau in the mathal district of sri  lanka lay the ruins of a 5th century  fortress of king kasyap  the shape and size of the rock jutting  out from the jungle below was created by  hardened lava from an extinct volcano  which dates back to prehistoric times  the rock formation has come to be known  by the name segedia or lion rock after  the large stone lion that once marked  the entrance to the staircase  visitors climbing to the top should  prepare for the 1200 steps it will take  to scale cigaria  to distract from the steep climb  visitors can study the 1500 year old  frescoes painted all along the rocks  at the top are the abandoned remains of  the king's fortress along with an  incredible view of what are believed to  be some of the oldest landscape gardens  in the world  it's a long climb but once at the top  you'll be experiencing what is referred  to by locals as the eighth wonder of the  world  [Music]  you
 

